 "how": "Every parlay the Live Parlays page shows. The page only reads this file, so changing it here changes what every device sees on its next load. A leg needs: game (an index into games below), player (spelled as ESPN spells him), team, stat, line, side (over or under), and main (true for a book main line like 43.5, false for a 'N+' threshold). Stats: passing_yards, passing_tds, passing_interceptions, attempts, completions, carries, rushing_yards, receptions, receiving_yards, targets, scrim_yards, any_td, fg_made, fg_att, kick_pts, and ml or ats for a whole-game bet, total for the game's points. A whole-game bet takes line 0 (the spread for ats), team set to the side you are on, and player set to whatever you want it called; a total takes the line and side over or under.",
